A module whose production code imports a package below its vendor directory by
the module's own path, and a package below testdata whose last element is
vendor. The go command refuses the first, telling the module to import the
vendored path as the vendored module's own, so no build compiles that package
and the platform its file names derives no configuration. A vendor element that
ends the path is a package of its own to the go command, so the build compiles
the second and its file's platform derives a configuration.

-- go.mod --
module example.com/app

go 1.27.0
-- main.go --
package main

import (
	"example.com/app/testdata/vendor"
	"example.com/app/vendor/helper"
)

func main() {
	helper.Run()
	vendor.Run()
}
-- vendor/helper/helper_windows.go --
package helper

// Run runs nothing.
func Run() {}
-- testdata/vendor/vendor.go --
package vendor

// Run runs nothing.
func Run() {}
-- testdata/vendor/vendor_plan9.go --
package vendor
